C2 phase 5b — the compactor gate opens: partition ownership above the fence
2026-08-24 · one all-node (ingest, own compaction off) + two compactors
             sharing one object store (deploy/compose/timelakedb-compactor-cluster.yml)
             driven by deploy/compose/compactor-drill/shard_drill.sh
================================================================================

THE CLAIM UNDER TEST: with the gate open, N compactors DIVIDE the partitions
instead of racing every one of them. Each owns a disjoint slice by FNV-1a over
db\0table\0partition mod N (compaction::owns_partition), computing its ordinal
by sorting its id with the discovered peers. The commit fence stays the
correctness floor; ownership is the efficiency layer that let the gate open.

What a green run shows, in order:
  - both compactors START (the gate is open — neither exits 2) and read their
    ordinal from discovery: ca=0, cb=1, count=2;
  - they DIVIDE: 8 tables split 4/4, both compactors busy;
  - no merge is WASTED: stale_merges stays 0 — no partition touched twice;
  - the store SETTLES: 8 tables -> 8 files, every partition compacted once;
  - nothing is LOST: 48 rows in, 48 rows out.

